# Security headers for static hosts that honour a _headers file
# (Netlify, Cloudflare Pages). Host-agnostic, and silently ignored by every host
# that does not read this format, so it is a convenience for self-hosters rather
# than this site's protection: real response headers are the deployment's job.
#
# The <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"> in src/layouts/Base.astro
# carries this policy minus frame-ancestors, which a meta CSP ignores. It is not
# an equivalent fallback either way: X-Frame-Options and X-Content-Type-Options
# cannot be set by meta at all. Clickjacking and nosniff protection therefore
# only exist where these are served as response headers.
#
# The policy below is first-party only, matching a site built with no analytics.
# A deployment that turns analytics on adds that vendor's hosts to its own
# response headers, next to the build values that enable the script.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Link: </llms.txt>; rel="describedby"; type="text/markdown", </sitemap-index.xml>; rel="sitemap"
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'
